Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Reconstruct Phase 1 stats provenance scripts

Add the two scripts the data-file headers reference but that were never
committed:

- scripts/compute_stats.py: reads the raw response DB and emits tourStats.json
  (means, SD, n, 95% CI, Welch's t / df / p, Cohen's d for the six pleasure
  metrics) plus src/data/phase1_frozen.json (canonical headline table).
  Parses the 1-5 rating from responses.value_text (full sample) instead of the
  sparsely populated value_num column (~30% subset) -- the root cause of the
  contradictory published means. Stdlib only; self-contained Student-t.
- scripts/freeze_phase1.js: --check (CI-safe) verifies tourData.js PLEASURE_METRICS
  and data.js avg objects match the computed snapshot, --write stamps them.

Regenerates tourStats.json from the 501-respondent snapshot, replacing the
stale 816-row artifact whose t/df/p did not match the displayed means.
Does not modify tourData.js or data.js (canonical-dataset choice left to the
author); run `node scripts/freeze_phase1.js --write` to apply.

